# Audit Logging — Universal Policy

**Rule: If it happened, it must be logged.** See `docs/universal-logging-policy.md` for full matrix.

## Always Audit (Audit DB — append-only)

| Category | Examples |
|---|---|
| **Auth** | Login, logout, failed login, password change, token refresh, lockout |
| **RBAC** | Role/permission changes, access denied (403) |
| **Writes** | Every command — Create, Update, Delete, BulkUpdate, StatusChange |
| **Sensitive reads** | Student profile, fee ledger, documents, financial records |
| **Exports** | Reports, CSV, PDF receipts, audit export |
| **Financial** | Payments, voids, journal post/reverse — highest priority |
| **Files** | Upload, download, delete |
| **Events** | Published, consumed, failed, dead-lettered |
| **Jobs** | Started, completed, failed |
| **Super admin** | All platform/tenant lifecycle actions |

## Operational Log (Serilog — every request)

- All HTTP requests via `RequestLoggingMiddleware` (method, path, status, elapsed)
- Validation failures, Result failures, exceptions
- Never log passwords, tokens, or unmasked PII

## Implementation

```csharp
// Writes — automatic via AuditBehavior on all ICommand
[AuditCategory("Student")]
public record UpdateStudentCommand(...) : ICommand<Result<Unit>>;

// Sensitive reads — AuditReadBehavior or explicit
[AuditRead("Student", nameof(GetStudentByIdQuery))]
public record GetStudentByIdQuery(Guid Id) : IQuery<Result<StudentDto>>;

// Access denied — in AuthorizationBehavior
await _auditService.LogAsync(AuditAction.AccessDenied, ...);

// Exports — in handler before returning file
await _auditService.LogAsync(AuditAction.Export, entityType, filters);
```

## AuditEntry Required Fields

`TenantId`, `UserId`, `Action`, `Category`, `EntityType`, `EntityId?`, `Description`, `BeforeJson?`, `AfterJson?`, `MetadataJson?`, `IpAddress`, `UserAgent`, `CorrelationId`, `Source`, `Outcome`, `CreatedAt`

## Do NOT

- Skip audit because "it's just a read" — if PII/financial, audit it
- Delete or update audit records
- Log audit writes through AuditBehavior (direct insert — loop prevention)
- Log passwords/tokens in any log layer

## Tests Required

- Handler test: verify `IAuditService.LogAsync` called (writes)
- Integration test: audit row exists after API call
- Architecture test: all `ICommand` have audit coverage
